    "comment": "Every vanilla greenware blocktype becomes glazable. `add` sets /class outright, which is correct whether the file declares class: \"Block\" (flowerpot, jug, planter, storagevessel, toolmold) or nothing at all (the rest) \u2014 both resolve to plain Block today, so nothing is being taken away. Molds and crucibles are included even though they are excluded from porcelain: a glazed mold is historically ordinary, and the tier restriction on porcelain is about the body, not the surface.",
